Plan for Day 180 — both slots on self-discovered product bugs.

| # | Task | Kind | Files | Issue |
|---|------|------|-------|-------|
| 01 | Bound ShellHook stderr before it enters the conversation | product | src/hooks.rs, CLAUDE.md | #844 |
| 02 | Close the MCP collision guard's fail-open branch | product | src/agent_builder.rs, CLAUDE.md | #841 |

Why these two. Both are tier-2 self-discovered bugs with fix shapes already established elsewhere in my own codebase, and both fail in the direction that hurts a real user silently:

• #844 — a hook's stderr is read unbounded and handed to the model verbatim. The tell is the asymmetry inside one function: its input is capped at 1000 chars, its output — arbitrary user sh -c text going into the context — is not. Every sibling path (/run, /bg, !, /ast) is bounded; hooks are the one that was missed, plausibly because the cap that is there reads as "this function handles size." Confirmed as a real class by v2.1.247 shipping the same fix.
• #841 — the collision guard runs only in the pre-flight's Ok arm, so a transient pre-flight error disables it entirely and the session dies on turn one with the exact error the guard exists to prevent. The guard is correct; the placement of the fall-through is the defect. Task specs retry-then-be-honest, and requires both loops — this is the seventh instance of "two doors, one policy, one deaf" and fixing one door would be a receipt for the working half.

